---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
import CTA from '../../../components/CTA.astro';
import SystemePlanLimits from '../../../components/SystemePlanLimits.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';

const product = await getEntry('products', 'systeme-io');
if (!product?.data.affiliateUrl || !product.data.hasAffiliateRelationship) throw new Error('Missing verified Systeme.io affiliate configuration.');

const title = 'Systeme.io Pricing (2026): Plans, Costs & Which Plan to Choose';
const description = 'Systeme.io plans start at $0. We verified current plan limits and compare Free, Startup, Webinar and Unlimited to help you choose the right tier.';
const canonical = '/pricing/systeme-io/';
const disclosure = 'SelectVerdict may earn a commission from qualifying signups through links on this page, at no additional cost to you. Affiliate relationships do not determine our conclusions.';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does Systeme.io cost?', a: 'The main public pricing page currently lists Free at $0, Startup at $17/month, Webinar at $47/month and Unlimited at $97/month. We found other official pages displaying $27 for Startup, so verify the checkout price.' },
  { q: 'Is Systeme.io free?', a: 'Yes. Systeme.io currently offers a continuing Free plan subject to plan limits.' },
  { q: 'Which paid Systeme.io plan is cheapest?', a: 'Startup is the lowest paid tier.' },
  { q: 'Does Startup include webinars?', a: 'Our September 2026 account matrix displays zero webinars for Startup and 10 for Webinar.' },
  { q: 'Should I pay annually?', a: 'Annual pricing currently represents two months’ equivalent saving versus twelve monthly payments, based on the main displayed prices.' },
];
const schema = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: 'Systeme.io Pricing (2026): Which Plan Do You Actually Need?', description, mainEntityOfPage: new URL(canonical, Astro.site).href, author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SelectVerdict' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SelectVerdict' } },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map(({ q, a }) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })) },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Software', href: '/software/' }, { label: 'Systeme.io Pricing' }]} />
  <article>
    <header class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Pricing guide</p><h1>Systeme.io Pricing (2026): Which Plan Do You Actually Need?</h1><p class="lede">A verified comparison of Systeme.io’s Free, Startup, Webinar and Unlimited tiers—and the operating limits that can force an upgrade before contact capacity does.</p><p class="meta">Account limits verified September 6, 2026</p></div></header>
    <div class="narrow prose article-body">
      <AffiliateDisclosure hasRelationship text={disclosure} />
      <p>Systeme.io has four main plan levels, starting with a permanent Free tier and progressing through Startup, Webinar and Unlimited.</p>
      <p>But choosing a plan isn't as simple as comparing contact limits.</p>
      <p>Our September 2026 account audit found that funnels, automation rules, workflows, campaigns, courses, domains and webinars can determine when you need to upgrade — sometimes long before you reach your contact limit.</p>
      <p>There is also an important pricing inconsistency worth knowing about: Systeme.io's current main public pricing page lists Startup at $17/month, while other official Systeme.io pages still display $27/month.</p>
      <p>Until Systeme.io clarifies the discrepancy, we recommend verifying the final checkout price before paying.</p>

      <h2>Systeme.io Pricing at a Glance</h2>
      <p>At the time of our September 2026 check, the main public pricing page listed:</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Systeme.io monthly pricing"><table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Monthly price</th><th>Contacts</th><th>Best suited to</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Free</th><td>$0</td><td>2,000</td><td>Testing and simple businesses</td></tr><tr><th>Startup</th><td>$17*</td><td>5,000</td><td>Small businesses needing more operating capacity</td></tr><tr><th>Webinar</th><td>$47</td><td>10,000</td><td>Businesses needing webinars or substantially higher limits</td></tr><tr><th>Unlimited</th><td>$97</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Larger or more complex operations</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <p><small>*We found other official Systeme.io pages displaying $27 for Startup. Check the final price shown during signup.</small></p>
      <p>Annual billing is currently advertised at the equivalent of ten monthly payments:</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Systeme.io annual pricing"><table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>12 months paid monthly</th><th>Annual price</th><th>Calculated saving</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Startup</th><td>$204</td><td>$170</td><td>$34</td></tr><tr><th>Webinar</th><td>$564</td><td>$470</td><td>$94</td></tr><tr><th>Unlimited</th><td>$1,164</td><td>$970</td><td>$194</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <p>These savings are our arithmetic based on the prices displayed on the main pricing page.</p>

      <h2>The Plan Limits We Verified</h2>
      <p>Price isn't the whole decision.</p><p>On September 6, 2026, we inspected the plan matrix displayed inside our Systeme.io account.</p>
      <SystemePlanLimits />
      <p class="source-note"><strong>Source:</strong> SelectVerdict account audit, September 6, 2026. Plan limits can change.</p>

      <h2>Free: Best for Validation</h2>
      <p>Free isn't merely a short trial.</p><p>It gives you enough infrastructure to operate a simple system: up to 2,000 contacts, three funnels, a website, custom domain, course, creator store and basic marketing automation.</p><p>Its most important restrictions aren't necessarily contacts.</p><p>Free gives you only:</p><p><strong>1 automation rule, 1 workflow, 1 tag and 1 email campaign.</strong></p><p>A simple business can fit comfortably. A more segmented marketing operation can outgrow Free with far fewer than 2,000 contacts.</p><p>Our <a href="/guides/systeme-io-free-plan/">hands-on guide to the Free plan</a> explains what those limits mean in practice.</p>

      <CTA title="Start with the $0 tier" text="Build and test a real system before deciding whether a paid plan is necessary." href={product.data.affiliateUrl} label="Try Systeme.io Free" affiliate />

      <h2>Startup: More Operating Room</h2>
      <p>Startup is where the architecture becomes substantially less restrictive.</p><p>Our account currently displays:</p><ul><li>5,000 contacts;</li><li>10 funnels;</li><li>50 funnel steps;</li><li>10 automation rules;</li><li>5 workflows;</li><li>10 campaigns;</li><li>5 courses;</li><li>3 custom domains.</li></ul><p>For many small businesses, the main reason to choose Startup isn't simply the extra 3,000 contacts.</p><p>It's the ability to operate several campaigns, automations and assets instead of one basic setup.</p>
      <h2>Webinar: A Genuine Feature Boundary</h2><p>Webinar increases capacity substantially:</p><ul><li>10,000 contacts;</li><li>50 funnels;</li><li>300 funnel steps;</li><li>100 automation rules;</li><li>20 workflows;</li><li>100 campaigns.</li></ul><p>More importantly, our account displays 10 webinars on this tier while Free and Startup display zero.</p><p>If webinars are central to your business, this creates a clear plan boundary rather than just a capacity upgrade.</p>
      <h2>Unlimited: Remove the Capacity Problem</h2><p>The highest tier removes the displayed numerical limits across the matrix we inspected.</p><p>At $97/month on the current main pricing page, it makes the most sense when managing multiple limits has itself become a recurring problem.</p><p>A small business shouldn't choose Unlimited simply because it sounds safer.</p><p>If Startup comfortably accommodates your operation, paying for unused unlimited capacity doesn't improve the economics.</p>

      <h2>Which Systeme.io Plan Should You Choose?</h2><p>A better approach than choosing by plan name is to identify the first resource your actual business will exceed.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Systeme.io plan selection examples"><table><thead><tr><th>Example</th><th>Likely minimum tier</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One simple funnel and email sequence</td><td>Free</td><td>Fits basic limits</td></tr><tr><td>Four funnels</td><td>Startup</td><td>Free allows 3</td></tr><tr><td>Several campaigns/automations</td><td>Startup</td><td>Free marketing limits are restrictive</td></tr><tr><td>3,000 contacts</td><td>Startup</td><td>Free allows 2,000</td></tr><tr><td>More than 5 workflows</td><td>Webinar</td><td>Startup allows 5</td></tr><tr><td>Evergreen webinar operation</td><td>Webinar</td><td>Lower tiers display 0 webinars</td></tr><tr><td>More than 10,000 contacts</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Webinar caps contacts at 10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Repeatedly hitting several limits</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Removes capacity management</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <p>The practical rule is:</p><p><strong>Choose the cheapest plan that accommodates the system you actually need.</strong></p><p>Don't pay for theoretical future complexity.</p>

      <h2>What About the $10,000 Free-Plan Revenue Limit?</h2><p>Our September account audit displays:</p><p><strong>Revenue from sales limit: $10,000 on Free</strong></p><p>and:</p><p><strong>Unlimited on all paid tiers.</strong></p><p>We have not generated $10,000 through the test account, so we haven't independently verified what happens at the threshold.</p><p>We therefore don't claim that Systeme.io automatically blocks sales at exactly $10,000.</p><p>We can verify only that the limit is currently displayed in the account.</p>
      <h2>Monthly or Annual?</h2><p>If you're already confident you'll use Systeme.io for a year, annual billing is mathematically cheaper at the prices currently displayed.</p><p>But a new user doesn't necessarily need to make that commitment immediately.</p><p>Because a permanent Free tier exists, you can first build and test a real system before deciding whether annual billing makes sense.</p>
      <h2>Our Pricing Verdict</h2><p>Free is the logical starting point for validation and simple operations.</p><p>Startup is primarily an upgrade in operating flexibility, not merely contact capacity.</p><p>Webinar becomes compelling when you need substantially higher limits or webinars.</p><p>Unlimited is for operations where multiple capacity limits have become recurring constraints.</p><p>The strongest pricing characteristic of Systeme.io isn't any single price.</p><p>It's the ability to start at $0 and upgrade only when a specific operating limit gives you a reason to pay.</p><p>For a broader assessment of the platform and the boundaries of our testing, read our <a href="/reviews/systeme-io/">full Systeme.io review</a>.</p>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map(({ q, a }) => <section><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></section>)}
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .article-body { padding-block: 3rem 5rem; }
  .article-body > :global(*) + :global(*) { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .article-body > :global(.disclosure) { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .article-body > :global(.cta) { margin-block: 3rem; }
  .source-note { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  table { width: 100%; min-width: 38rem; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  th, td { padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  thead th { background: var(--surface-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody tr:last-child > * { border-bottom: 0; }
</style>
